    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0271" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/5–445</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and the Secretary of the Navy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Forrestal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-04">4 May 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Joint Chiefs of Staff
                    concur in the recommendation of General Eisenhower in the attached copy of his
                    cable on the subject of the French zone in Germany and recommend that it be used
                    as a basis for negotiation in the European Advisory Commission. The Joint Chiefs
                    of Staff consider that the bridgehead of the Rhine east of Koblenz in the State
                    of Hessen-Nassau comprising Unterwester Waldkreis, Unterlahn Kreis and Sankt
                    Goarshausen Kreis should be given to the French if they ask for it.</p>
                <p>This decision supersedes the remarks in the last two sentences of paragraph 7<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi> (3) and paragraph 8 of the letter dispatched to
                    the Secretary of State by the Secretaries of War and the Navy on 1 May 1945 on
                    this matter.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d209-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H <hi rendition="#small-caps">Struve Hensel</hi>
                    </signed><anchor n="4" xml:id="d209-f2"/>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of War</hi>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d209-a1.xml" xpointer="d209-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
